{{~##
   One declared record type, and the levels inside it that are its own.

   **A struct is an entity beside a table and an enum, so it gets a file like one.** The
   declaration says "this is one type", and the generated code says the same thing only if
   there is one type. spec/types/declared-struct-identity.md.

   The body is the same include a record class uses for a group nobody declared. It is written
   for the nested case, which is one level deeper than a type at file level - so the outermost
   is captured and dedented rather than kept twice, and the levels inside it stay nested where
   the include already puts them. **This language allows one public type per file**, so those
   levels cannot become files of their own or siblings beside it.
##~}}
{{ include 'java-file-head.sbn' ~}}
{{~## The levels inside, at the indent the include already writes them at. ##~}}
{{~ capture inner ~}}
{{~ for rt in record.types ~}}
{{~ if !for.last }}
    /** A record inside {{ record.name }}. */
{{ include 'java-record-body.sbn' ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~## And the type itself, which the model puts last. ##~}}
{{~ for rt in record.types ~}}
{{~ if for.last ~}}
{{~ if record.comment | array.size > 0 ~}}
{{~ for line in record.comment ~}}
/** {{ line }} */
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ else ~}}
/** One value of the declaration that names it. */
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ capture body ~}}
{{ include 'java-record-body.sbn' ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~## One replace: the four-space pattern matches the front of every deeper line as well, so
      each loses one level. A newline goes in front so the first line is reached the same way
      as the rest, and comes off again after. ##~}}
{{~## `static` goes with the nesting: a file-level type cannot carry it. ##~}}
{{~ open = ("
" + body) | string.replace("
    ", "
") | string.replace("public static final class", "public final class") | string.slice 1 | string.rstrip ~}}
{{~## The closing brace comes off so the levels inside go in ahead of it. ##~}}
{{ open | string.slice 0 (open.size - 1) | string.rstrip }}
{{~ inner ~}}
}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
